Lost update on stock: check-then-write instead of a conditional decrement.

reserve() reads the stock, checks it in Go and writes back the computed
value. Under READ COMMITTED two transactions read the same stock, both pass
the check and both write stock-1, so concurrent orders sell the same unit
twice. The fix in main is one statement:
UPDATE ... SET stock = stock - $qty WHERE id = $id AND stock >= $qty.

Expect-Fail: TestConcurrentOrdersNeverOversell

